<%# The compact metadata a record's identity card ends with: a set of
    `label: value` pairs, optionally carrying an explanation behind a popover.

    This is the treatment for a fact that is a *property of the record's own
    plumbing* rather than information a reader scans for. "scope: universe" and
    "color: #d3d3d3" belong on one quiet line at the bottom of the card, not in
    the labelled facts grid above it: the grid is what a reader reads, and these
    two are the record's settings.

    `facts` is a list of hashes, each with:
      text       - the whole rendered pair, already a complete locale-written
                   string, so neither a label nor a value is spliced into a
                   sentence here;
      hint       - the longer explanation, shown in a popover (optional);
      hint_label - the popover's title and the trigger's accessible name, which
                   is what a screen reader announces for a control with no
                   visible text of its own. Required with `hint`. %>
<% facts = local_assigns.fetch(:facts) %>
<% if facts.present? %>
  <div class="detail-footer">
    <% facts.each do |fact| %>
      <span class="detail-footer-item">
        <%= fact.fetch(:text) %>
        <% if fact[:hint].present? %>
          <%# `hover focus click` because a touch pointer never hovers, and the
              same trigger set the Timeline's node popovers use. %>
          <button type="button" class="detail-footer-hint"
            data-controller="popover"
            data-popover-content-value="<%= fact.fetch(:hint) %>"
            data-popover-title-value="<%= fact.fetch(:hint_label) %>"
            data-bs-trigger="hover focus click"
            data-bs-placement="top"
            data-bs-custom-class="custom-popover"
            aria-label="<%= fact.fetch(:hint_label) %>">
            <i class="bi bi-info-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          </button>
        <% end %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>